{
  "id": "pythagoras-ladder",
  "title": "Pythagorean theorem ↔ a ladder on a wall",
  "category": "Maths",
  "width": 960,
  "height": 680,
  "background": "grid",
  "learning": {
    "goal": "See that in any right triangle the two short sides squared add up to the long side squared, and use it to know how high a ladder reaches.",
    "question": "A 6 m ladder must reach a window 5.5 m above the ground. How far from the wall can its foot be?",
    "answer": "The ladder is the long side, so a² + 5.5² = 6². That gives a² = 36 − 30.25 = 5.75, so a ≈ 2.40 m. Any closer and it still reaches; farther and it falls short.",
    "caveat": "This assumes the wall is exactly vertical and the ground exactly flat (a true right angle) and treats the ladder as a thin line. The 'foot at a quarter of the length' rule is a common ladder-safety guideline (e.g. OSHA's 4-to-1 rule), shown here as an example."
  },
  "params": {
    "a": {
      "label": "foot of the ladder from the wall (m)",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 4,
      "step": 0.25,
      "value": 3
    }
  },
  "vars": {
    "s": 40,
    "gx": 300,
    "gy": 420,
    "h": "sqrt(25 - a^2)",
    "A": "a * s",
    "H": "h * s",
    "fx": "gx + A",
    "ty": "gy - H",
    "a2": "a^2",
    "h2": "h^2"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        40,
        70
      ],
      "text": "How high does a 5 m ladder reach?",
      "size": 42,
      "chapter": "The question",
      "say": "You lean a 5 metre ladder on a wall. How high does it reach? It depends on where you put its foot."
    },
    {
      "type": "line",
      "from": [
        300,
        120
      ],
      "to": [
        300,
        420
      ],
      "style": {
        "width": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        314,
        150
      ],
      "text": "wall",
      "size": 26,
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "line",
      "from": [
        70,
        420
      ],
      "to": [
        620,
        420
      ],
      "style": {
        "width": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        620,
        460
      ],
      "text": "ground",
      "size": 26,
      "anchor": "end",
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "line",
      "from": [
        "fx - h",
        "gy + a"
      ],
      "to": [
        "gx - h",
        "ty + a"
      ],
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C",
        "width": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "line",
      "from": [
        "fx + h",
        "gy - a"
      ],
      "to": [
        "gx + h",
        "ty - a"
      ],
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C",
        "width": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "repeat",
      "times": 9,
      "step": {
        "type": "line",
        "from": [
          "fx - (i + 1) / 10 * A - 1.8 * h",
          "gy - (i + 1) / 10 * H + 1.8 * a"
        ],
        "to": [
          "fx - (i + 1) / 10 * A + 1.8 * h",
          "gy - (i + 1) / 10 * H - 1.8 * a"
        ],
        "style": {
          "color": "#C8442C",
          "width": 2
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "polyline",
      "points": [
        [
          300,
          398
        ],
        [
          322,
          398
        ],
        [
          322,
          420
        ]
      ],
      "style": {
        "width": 2.2
      },
      "chapter": "Take it apart",
      "say": "Wall, ground and ladder make a triangle, and the corner where the wall meets the ground is a right angle."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        "gx + A / 2",
        "gy + A + 36"
      ],
      "text": "a = {a:2} m",
      "size": 26,
      "anchor": "middle",
      "style": {
        "color": "#2F5BEA"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        "gx - H - 14",
        "gy - H / 2 + 9"
      ],
      "text": "h",
      "size": 30,
      "anchor": "end",
      "style": {
        "color": "#2E8F62"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        170
      ],
      "text": "ladder: 5 m (fixed)",
      "size": 26,
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        210
      ],
      "text": "foot: a = {a:2} m",
      "size": 26,
      "style": {
        "color": "#2F5BEA"
      },
      "say": "The ladder never changes: 5 metres. What you choose is a, the distance of the foot from the wall."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        250
      ],
      "text": "height: h = {h:2} m",
      "size": 26,
      "style": {
        "color": "#2E8F62"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "polygon",
      "points": [
        [
          "gx",
          "gy"
        ],
        [
          "fx",
          "gy"
        ],
        [
          "fx",
          "gy + A"
        ],
        [
          "gx",
          "gy + A"
        ]
      ],
      "style": {
        "color": "#2F5BEA",
        "width": 2.4,
        "fill": "#2F5BEA",
        "fillStyle": "hachure",
        "opacity": 0.8
      },
      "chapter": "The idea",
      "say": "Now build a square on each side. On the ground, a square of side a."
    },
    {
      "type": "polygon",
      "points": [
        [
          "gx - H",
          "ty"
        ],
        [
          "gx",
          "ty"
        ],
        [
          "gx",
          "gy"
        ],
        [
          "gx - H",
          "gy"
        ]
      ],
      "style": {
        "color": "#2E8F62",
        "width": 2.4,
        "fill": "#2E8F62",
        "fillStyle": "hachure",
        "opacity": 0.8
      },
      "say": "On the wall, a square of side h."
    },
    {
      "type": "polygon",
      "points": [
        [
          "fx",
          "gy"
        ],
        [
          "gx",
          "ty"
        ],
        [
          "gx + H",
          "ty - A"
        ],
        [
          "fx + H",
          "gy - A"
        ]
      ],
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C",
        "width": 2.4,
        "fill": "#C8442C",
        "fillStyle": "hachure",
        "opacity": 0.6
      },
      "say": "And on the ladder, a square of side 5. Here is the surprise: the two small squares together have exactly the area of the big one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        "(fx + gx) / 2 + H / 2",
        "(gy + ty) / 2 - A / 2 + 10"
      ],
      "text": "5 m",
      "size": 30,
      "anchor": "middle",
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        330
      ],
      "text": "a² + h² = 5²",
      "size": 36,
      "id": "rule"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        380
      ],
      "text": "{a2:2} + {h2:2} = 25",
      "size": 28,
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      },
      "say": "Move the foot of the ladder: the blue and green squares trade area, but their sum is always 25."
    },
    {
      "type": "highlight",
      "from": [
        636,
        320
      ],
      "to": [
        852,
        320
      ],
      "thickness": 30,
      "chapter": "The close",
      "say": "So the height is the square root of 25 minus a squared. Move the foot closer, and the ladder climbs higher."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        470
      ],
      "text": "safety rule of thumb:",
      "size": 26,
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        510
      ],
      "text": "foot = 5 ÷ 4 = 1.25 m",
      "size": 26
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        640,
        550
      ],
      "text": "→ it reaches 4.84 m",
      "size": 26,
      "style": {
        "color": "#2E8F62"
      },
      "say": "Ladder guides say: put the foot a quarter of the length away. Set a to 1.25 and check that h is about 4.84."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en-US"
}